/*
 * Samsung Galaxy Note 8 (greatlte, SM-N950N) board DT, part "l7":
 * L7 power management: idle states, suspend, PDN (L7 4).
 *
 * Included at the end of exynos8895-greatlte.dts, after L0's nodes, in the merge
 * order of FULL_IMAGE_PLAN.md 2.2. Owner: WP-L7; no other work package edits this
 * file (plan 2.3 rule D1). A node that two parts both configure (&usi9, &usi10)
 * is written identically in both files: dtc lets the later file win on a differing
 * value, which gl-verify V-DUP reports as an error. L0's reserved-memory stays in
 * the .dts; carveout additions and flag changes are &label edits here (plan X-8).
 */

/*
 * L7 4.2: the arch counter does not tick in SLEEP. Stock removed
 * CLOCK_SOURCE_SUSPEND_NONSTOP from the arch counter and takes the sleep time
 * from rtc0 (S:drivers/clocksource/arm_arch_timer.c:455-461; IK:3889-3890);
 * 6.18 sets NONSTOP unless this property is present
 * (A:drivers/clocksource/arm_arch_timer.c:940-941,1177-1178). The node has no
 * label (A:arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos8895.dtsi:1358). always-on is not
 * added: the arch timer is in the core and stops in C2, C3STOP stays. Spec
 * O7-3: if P12 shows the counter runs in SLEEP, the property may be dropped.
 */
&{/timer} {
	arm,no-tick-in-suspend;
};
